    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0385" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg289"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 68.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have but little time to prepare this
                    dispatch, as the steamer sails from here in less than an hour. The Santo Domingo
                    mail has just reached me. I inclose copy of General Heureaux’s letter in
                    reference to the Ozama River bridge incident. I know from personal observation
                    that there is at this time very little money, and that it is impossible for them
                    to pay the whole sum in cash.</p>
                <p>I also send inclosed draft for the expenses of Mr. Noble for $1,489.02, sent by
                    the President, draft No. 10137 on Muller, Schall &amp; Go.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d189-a1.xml" xpointer="d189-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
